1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:02,830
Every team has had this moment: wait,

2
00:00:02,870 --> 00:00:05,880
didn't we already decide not to do that?

3
00:00:05,920 --> 00:00:07,800
Precedent is a decision

4
00:00:07,840 --> 00:00:08,840
memory that acts.

5
00:00:08,880 --> 00:00:10,360
It catches the contradiction in

6
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:13,200
Confluence, in Jira, in your workflow,

7
00:00:13,240 --> 00:00:16,110
and in your AI coding agent.

8
00:00:16,150 --> 00:00:18,690
It starts where teams already write.

9
00:00:18,730 --> 00:00:20,130
In this architecture review,

10
00:00:20,170 --> 00:00:21,570
the payments team decided,

11
00:00:21,610 --> 00:00:23,170
with a /decision,

12
00:00:23,210 --> 00:00:24,510
to keep all transactional

13
00:00:24,550 --> 00:00:26,730
payment data in PostgreSQL.

14
00:00:26,770 --> 00:00:28,760
Precedent captures it with its owner,

15
00:00:28,800 --> 00:00:30,960
date and rationale, and the page shows

16
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:33,240
which Jira work contradicts it.

17
00:00:35,811 --> 00:00:38,371
Months later, someone files new work:

18
00:00:38,411 --> 00:00:41,371
move payout reconciliation to MongoDB.

19
00:00:41,411 --> 00:00:43,951
Before they even press create, Jira's

20
00:00:43,991 --> 00:00:47,121
own create dialog warns them: already

21
00:00:47,161 --> 00:00:49,871
decided in DEC-1, with who decided,

22
00:00:49,911 --> 00:00:51,881
when, and what to use instead.

23
00:00:55,238 --> 00:00:56,918
If it is filed anyway,

24
00:00:56,958 --> 00:00:59,288
the Precedent panel flags the conflict,

25
00:00:59,328 --> 00:01:00,648
quotes the sentence that tripped

26
00:01:00,688 --> 00:01:01,988
the guardrail, and offers

27
00:01:02,028 --> 00:01:04,118
a one-click compliant alternative.

28
00:01:04,158 --> 00:01:05,828
Precedent also keeps a short brief

29
00:01:05,868 --> 00:01:07,438
for coding agents in the work item:

30
00:01:07,478 --> 00:01:09,368
what to do, which packages are denied,

31
00:01:09,408 --> 00:01:11,668
and which code the decision governs.

32
00:01:12,360 --> 00:01:14,520
And it is enforced in the workflow.

33
00:01:14,560 --> 00:01:16,520
Moving the work item to Done is blocked

34
00:01:16,560 --> 00:01:18,080
while the conflict is unresolved,

35
00:01:18,120 --> 00:01:19,280
unless the team reviews it

36
00:01:19,320 --> 00:01:20,990
or logs an exception.

37
00:01:24,515 --> 00:01:25,995
Ask Precedent hands the work

38
00:01:26,035 --> 00:01:27,475
item to the Rovo agent.

39
00:01:27,515 --> 00:01:29,635
It explains why the decision was made,

40
00:01:29,675 --> 00:01:31,845
who owns it, and the options: comply,

41
00:01:31,885 --> 00:01:34,235
log an exception, or supersede the

42
00:01:34,275 --> 00:01:36,505
decision, citing the source every time.

43
00:01:37,217 --> 00:01:39,557
Now a developer opens the work item

44
00:01:39,597 --> 00:01:41,497
in Claude Code, straight from Jira.

45
00:01:41,537 --> 00:01:42,977
Jira hands over the summary

46
00:01:43,017 --> 00:01:43,857
and the description,

47
00:01:43,897 --> 00:01:46,167
and with it, the Precedent brief.

48
00:01:49,216 --> 00:01:51,496
This is a real Claude Code session

49
00:01:51,536 --> 00:01:53,176
with exactly that prompt.

50
00:01:53,216 --> 00:01:55,096
Before writing a line of code, the agent

51
00:01:55,136 --> 00:01:59,376
stops: the task would break DEC-1.

52
00:01:59,416 --> 00:02:00,816
It reads the ledger code,

53
00:02:00,856 --> 00:02:03,056
explains why the decision exists,

54
00:02:03,096 --> 00:02:05,896
and proposes a PostgreSQL JSONB design

55
00:02:05,936 --> 00:02:07,366
instead, or an exception

56
00:02:07,406 --> 00:02:09,006
for the owner to approve.

57
00:02:19,652 --> 00:02:21,812
Decisions stay alive.

58
00:02:21,852 --> 00:02:24,042
Tripwires watch the assumptions

59
00:02:24,082 --> 00:02:25,632
behind them: when shared Redis

60
00:02:25,672 --> 00:02:28,262
incidents pile up, the Radar turns red

61
00:02:28,302 --> 00:02:30,692
and the owner is asked to review.

62
00:02:30,732 --> 00:02:32,852
Meeting notes feed a decision inbox,

63
00:02:32,892 --> 00:02:34,562
and Rovo Search finds every

64
00:02:34,602 --> 00:02:36,722
decision through the Teamwork Graph.

65
00:02:37,384 --> 00:02:39,164
Precedent. One Forge app that runs

66
00:02:39,204 --> 00:02:40,804
entirely on Atlassian,

67
00:02:40,844 --> 00:02:42,714
so your team, and your agents,

68
00:02:42,754 --> 00:02:44,834
know what has already been decided.

